ace is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Transfer to a new problem"}],"title":"Year 8, Week 34, Lesson 4: Probability problems","unit_number":9,"unit_title":"Probability experiments and simulations","week":34,"week_in_unit":2,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nExample for Probability problems: state the values, show the method step by step, and check the result. Weak: an answer with no working.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the places, values or distances used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Probability problems.","caption":"Check reasonableness.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Values</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">Probability problems</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Method</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">shown working</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Accurate method.","caption":"Name the skill.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Weak</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">no working</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Strong</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">steps + check</text></g></svg>"}],"year_level":"Year 8"}') WHERE seed_key='s4-mat-y8-w34-l4' AND family_id IS NULL;
